06-integrate-article — Patch-ready execution packet 1. Governing audit stance Freeze one immutable candidate SHA and audit that candidate, not a moving branch name. Treat every diff hunk, test, document sentence, screenshot, and lane report as a claim until independently tied to that SHA. The complete package scope is exactly eight paths. attachment-0002-029092777dbb1cc… The curated bundle does not contain the production bodies of CLAUDE.md, src/footer_popup.rs, or src/mcp_computer_use_tools.rs, so no conclusion about those files may be based on the attachment alone; the local frozen main...HEAD diff is authoritative. The package delta is dominated by src/footer_popup.rs, with the package totaling 769 insertions and 126 deletions. attachment-0003-0172a2f5f15c885… Use these evidence rules throughout: Shared components, theme/chrome tokens, and shared action authorities outrank surface-local implementations. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… Do not retune, normalize, “clean up,” or update expectations around locked glass motion. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… Every Cargo command goes through ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… A source-reading test proves source shape, not runtime behavior. The repository explicitly places those tests at the bottom of the enforcement ladder. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… A visual screenshot proves only the static pixels visible in that frame. It does not prove first-click delivery, keyboard routing, lifecycle, listener cardinality, animation, focus restoration, or temporal convergence. A lane summary is never proof. Accept its referenced raw diff, terminal receipt, runtime trace, JSON response, or screenshot only after matching the candidate SHA. 2. First implementation action Run this from the repository root. It freezes the audit identity, verifies the measured campaign baseline, and immediately produces the first evidence receipt. Bashset -euo pipefail LANE=".notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/06-integrate-article" mkdir -p "$LANE/receipts" BRANCH="$(git branch --show-current)" AUDIT_HEAD="$(git rev-parse HEAD)" AUDIT_BASE="$(git merge-base main "$AUDIT_HEAD")" COMMIT_COUNT="$(git rev-list --count "$AUDIT_BASE..$AUDIT_HEAD")" BRANCH_PATH_COUNT="$(git diff --name-only "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" | wc -l | tr -d ' ')" test "$BRANCH" = "consistency/default-recommendations" test "$COMMIT_COUNT" -eq 50 test "$BRANCH_PATH_COUNT" -eq 481 git -c color.ui=never diff \ --name-status \ --find-renames \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- \ CLAUDE.md \ GLOSSARY.md \ src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs \ src/footer_popup.rs \ src/list_item_tests.rs \ src/mcp_computer_use_tools.rs \ src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs \ src/warning_banner.rs \ | tee "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-name-status.txt" OWNED_ROWS="$(awk 'END { print NR }' "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-name-status.txt")" test "$OWNED_ROWS" -eq 8 git -c color.ui=never diff \ --shortstat \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- \ CLAUDE.md \ GLOSSARY.md \ src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs \ src/footer_popup.rs \ src/list_item_tests.rs \ src/mcp_computer_use_tools.rs \ src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs \ src/warning_banner.rs \ | tee "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-shortstat.txt" shasum -a 256 \ CLAUDE.md \ GLOSSARY.md \ src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs \ src/footer_popup.rs \ src/list_item_tests.rs \ src/mcp_computer_use_tools.rs \ src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs \ src/warning_banner.rs \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-production-sha-before.txt" Expected result: Current branch is exactly consistency/default-recommendations. Frozen candidate is 50 commits beyond its merge base. Branch-wide delta contains 481 paths. Package receipt contains exactly eight rows. Package shortstat reports eight files, 769 insertions, and 126 deletions. No production file has been edited. If any measured value differs, stop the package before interpreting source. Record CANDIDATE_DRIFT; do not silently audit a different branch state. Exact first audit-artifact write Immediately write: Bashcat > "$LANE/00-scope-and-identity.md" <<EOF # 06-integrate-article — candidate identity - Status: IN_PROGRESS - Branch: \`$BRANCH\` - Frozen HEAD: \`$AUDIT_HEAD\` - Merge base with main: \`$AUDIT_BASE\` - Commits in candidate range: $COMMIT_COUNT - Branch-wide changed paths: $BRANCH_PATH_COUNT - Package-owned changed paths: $OWNED_ROWS - Production edits authorized: no - Commit, push, merge, app deploy authorized: no - Shared article or integrated-ledger edits authorized here: no - Candidate authority: local \`git diff $AUDIT_BASE $AUDIT_HEAD\` - Evidence rule: runtime wording requires a real runtime boundary; source-reading tests remain static evidence. - Candidate drift rule: any later HEAD change invalidates unqualified receipts and must be reported. ## Owned paths 1. \`CLAUDE.md\` 2. \`GLOSSARY.md\` 3. \`src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs\` 4. \`src/footer_popup.rs\` 5. \`src/list_item_tests.rs\` 6. \`src/mcp_computer_use_tools.rs\` 7. \`src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs\` 8. \`src/warning_banner.rs\` EOF Also save the frozen variables for later commands: Bashcat > "$LANE/receipts/candidate.env" <<EOF AUDIT_HEAD=$AUDIT_HEAD AUDIT_BASE=$AUDIT_BASE EOF 3. Required lane artifact structure Create exactly this structure. No production or shared campaign file is written by this worker. .notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/06-integrate-article/ ├── 00-scope-and-identity.md ├── 01-path-accounting.tsv ├── 02-observed-improvements.md ├── 03-breakage-candidates.md ├── 04-proof-gaps.md ├── 05-verification-results.md ├── 06-runtime-matrix.md ├── 07-screenshot-requests.md ├── 08-article-hunks.md ├── 09-next-actions.md ├── 10-integration-reconciliation.md ├── integration-requests.jsonl ├── worker-report.md └── receipts/ ├── candidate.env ├── 00-owned-name-status.txt ├── 00-owned-shortstat.txt ├── 00-owned-production-sha-before.txt ├── 01-owned-numstat.txt ├── 02-owned-function-diff.patch ├── 03-owned-commit-provenance.tsv ├── 04-doc-word-diff.patch ├── 05-glossary-link-check.txt ├── 06-footer-symbol-map.txt ├── 07-footer-static-audit.txt ├── 08-source-audit-delta.txt ├── 09-list-item-tests.txt ├── 10-actions-source-audit-tests.txt ├── 11-quick-question-contract.txt ├── 12-portal-consumers.txt ├── 13-portal-tests.txt ├── 14-mcp-diff-and-consumers.txt ├── 15-mcp-tests.txt ├── 16-warning-banner-consumers.txt ├── 17-source-audit-ratchet.txt ├── 18-check-lib.txt ├── 19-runtime-footer-trace.jsonl ├── 20-runtime-elements-before.json ├── 21-runtime-elements-after.json ├── 22-runtime-result.md ├── 23-glass-antidrift.txt ├── 90-integrated-path-union.tsv ├── 91-integrated-path-gaps.txt ├── 92-integrated-path-duplicates.txt ├── 98-owned-production-sha-after.txt └── 99-final-status.txt Package screenshots, only when explicitly assigned, go under: .artifacts/branch-trust-audit/06-integrate-article/ 01-path-accounting.tsv schema Use a literal tab-delimited header: path base_blob head_blob numstat subsystem changed_symbols hunk_count disposition finding_ids proof_ids screenshot_ids confidence status One row per owned path. status may be only: AUDITED BLOCKED_CANDIDATE_DRIFT BLOCKED_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE PENDING, blank, or “looks fine” is not a completed row. disposition may be a comma-separated combination of: VERIFIED_IMPROVEMENT PLAUSIBLE_IMPROVEMENT BREAKAGE_CANDIDATE CONFIRMED_REGRESSION PROOF_GAP DOCUMENTATION_ONLY TEST_ONLY NO_MATERIAL_CHANGE Generate the initial blob and numstat data: Bashsource "$LANE/receipts/candidate.env" git -c color.ui=never diff \ --numstat \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- \ CLAUDE.md \ GLOSSARY.md \ src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs \ src/footer_popup.rs \ src/list_item_tests.rs \ src/mcp_computer_use_tools.rs \ src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs \ src/warning_banner.rs \ | tee "$LANE/receipts/01-owned-numstat.txt" git -c color.ui=never diff \ --histogram \ --find-renames \ --function-context \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- \ CLAUDE.md \ GLOSSARY.md \ src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs \ src/footer_popup.rs \ src/list_item_tests.rs \ src/mcp_computer_use_tools.rs \ src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs \ src/warning_banner.rs \ > "$LANE/receipts/02-owned-function-diff.patch" git -c color.ui=never log \ --reverse \ --date=iso-strict \ --format='%H%x09%ad%x09%an%x09%s' \ "$AUDIT_BASE..$AUDIT_HEAD" -- \ CLAUDE.md \ GLOSSARY.md \ src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs \ src/footer_popup.rs \ src/list_item_tests.rs \ src/mcp_computer_use_tools.rs \ src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs \ src/warning_banner.rs \ > "$LANE/receipts/03-owned-commit-provenance.tsv" 4. Ordered finite audit batch Work package 1 — Documentation authority and claim inventory Paths CLAUDE.md GLOSSARY.md Exact inspection Bashsource "$LANE/receipts/candidate.env" git -c color.ui=never diff \ --word-diff=plain \ --unified=12 \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- \ CLAUDE.md GLOSSARY.md \ > "$LANE/receipts/04-doc-word-diff.patch" git -c color.ui=never diff \ --unified=0 \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- GLOSSARY.md \ | rg '^[+-]\|' \ > "$LANE/receipts/04-glossary-changed-table-rows.txt" || true rg -n \ 'cargo (build|check|test|clippy)|agent-cargo|md flows/|Project Flows|GLOSSARY|glass|motion|source[- ]audit' \ CLAUDE.md AGENTS.md \ > "$LANE/receipts/04-claude-contract-scan.txt" || true CLAUDE.md audit For every changed sentence, answer: Does it direct agents to use bare Cargo? Does it direct work through disabled md flows/... execution? Does it contradict shared-component ownership? Does it imply source-reading tests are behavior proof? Does it duplicate a surface map that belongs in GLOSSARY.md? Does it weaken the “current source over stale notes” rule? Does it describe a runtime behavior without a receipt? Concrete failure scenarios: CLAUDE.md says cargo test → an agent contends on the shared target lock. CLAUDE.md says to dispatch a flow → the agent reports delegated progress that cannot be observed. CLAUDE.md says “footer clicks work” based only on source tests → article overstates confidence. CLAUDE.md describes a superseded file owner → later changes land in the wrong layer. A documentation contradiction is a real audit finding even when compilation passes. GLOSSARY.md audit The glossary currently describes the footer as native detached capsules below an eight-point gutter, with the footer and bounded GPUI stage inside the same NSWindow. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… Do not accept that as runtime proof. Verify each changed table row against candidate source and, for behavioral prose, against tests or runtime receipts. Run a frozen-candidate local-link and line-anchor check: Bashexport AUDIT_HEAD python3 - <<'PY' > "$LANE/receipts/05-glossary-link-check.txt" import os import re import subprocess import sys head = os.environ["AUDIT_HEAD"] def show(path: str) -> str: return subprocess.check_output( ["git", "show", f"{head}:{path}"], text=True, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, ) glossary = show("GLOSSARY.md") targets = re.findall(r"\]\(([^)]+)\)", glossary) checked = 0 issues: list[str] = [] for target in targets: if target.startswith(("http://", "https://", "#", "mailto:")): continue path, sep, anchor = target.partition("#") if not path: continue checked += 1 try: source = show(path) except subprocess.CalledProcessError: issues.append(f"MISSING\t{target}") continue if sep and anchor.startswith("L") and anchor[1:].isdigit(): requested = int(anchor[1:]) line_count = len(source.splitlines()) if requested < 1 or requested > line_count: issues.append( f"STALE_LINE\t{target}\trequested={requested}\tlines={line_count}" ) if issues: print("\n".join(issues)) print(f"FAIL: {len(issues)} issue(s) across {checked} local links") sys.exit(1) print(f"OK: {checked} local links; 0 missing paths; 0 stale numeric line anchors") PY Then inspect every changed glossary row as a semantic unit, not every line. Record: exact row heading; named symbol; source path exists; symbol exists at frozen HEAD; behavior claim and proof tier; stale or overstated wording; article-safe sentence. No changed row may be marked AUDITED merely because its Markdown link resolves. Work package 2 — Native footer architecture and action authority Paths src/footer_popup.rs src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs Related read-only files Inspect these because the changed tests name them as the actual dispatch and lifecycle owners: src/app_impl/ui_window.rs src/app_impl/actions_toggle.rs src/app_impl/startup.rs src/main_sections/render_impl.rs src/render_script_list/mod.rs src/components/launcher_ask_ai_hint.rs src/theme/opacity.rs src/platform/secondary_window_config.rs src/ui/chrome/tokens.rs Exact symbol inventory Bashsource "$LANE/receipts/candidate.env" { echo "## footer_popup.rs declarations" git show "$AUDIT_HEAD:src/footer_popup.rs" \ | rg -n \ '^\s*(pub(\([^)]*\))?\s+)?(unsafe\s+)?(extern\s+"C"\s+)?fn\s+|^\s*(pub(\([^)]*\))?\s+)?(struct|enum|type|const|static)\s+' echo echo "## cross-file footer authorities" for path in \ src/app_impl/ui_window.rs \ src/app_impl/actions_toggle.rs \ src/app_impl/startup.rs \ src/main_sections/render_impl.rs \ src/render_script_list/mod.rs do echo "### $path" git show "$AUDIT_HEAD:$path" \ | rg -n \ 'FooterAction|MainWindowFooterConfig|FooterButtonConfig|footer_action_channel|ensure_main_footer_action_listener|sync_main_footer_popup|handle_main_footer_action|dispatch_main_window_footer_action|main_window_footer_config_with_cx|standard_main_window_footer_buttons|dispatch_actions_toggle_for_current_view|handle_cmd_k_actions_toggle|try_run_ready_agent_chat_script|paste_latest_agent_chat_response_to_frontmost|open_tab_ai_agent_chat_with_entry_intent' \ || true done } > "$LANE/receipts/06-footer-symbol-map.txt" The audit must explicitly cover these known symbols when present: FooterAction FooterAction::Run FooterAction::Actions FooterAction::Ai FooterAction::PasteResponse FooterButtonConfig MainWindowFooterConfig footer_action_channel ScriptKitFooterButton footer_button_class footer_button_accepts_first_mouse footer_button_mouse_down_can_move_window make_footer_hint_item footer_hit_test footer_item_button_at_point footer_button_in_subviews nearest_footer_item_button footer_passthrough_view_class footer_passthrough_hit_test install_footer_host_view FOOTER_HINTS_ID handle_main_footer_action dispatch_main_window_footer_action standard_main_window_footer_buttons ensure_main_footer_action_listener sync_main_footer_popup main_window_footer_config_with_cx Required static audit Write 07-footer-static-audit.txt with one explicit PASS, FAIL, or UNVERIFIED row for each item: Config ownership Footer labels, shortcuts, enabled state, visibility, and action are derived from MainWindowFooterConfig. No second local footer-action model exists. Canonical dispatch Native footer clicks and GPUI footer rail clicks converge on dispatch_main_window_footer_action. Actions do not bypass dispatch_actions_toggle_for_current_view. FooterAction::Run handles Agent Chat’s ready-script path before normal execute_selected. FooterAction::PasteResponse invokes only the latest assistant-response paste path. FooterAction::Ai uses an entry intent appropriate for a clean quick question. Listener cardinality ensure_main_footer_action_listener cannot install multiple listeners after repeated calls to sync_main_footer_popup. The listener is cancelled or dropped with the owning application/window lifecycle. One channel event cannot dispatch twice. View/config guarding Hidden, stale, or unsupported buttons cannot dispatch. Mini/full/Agent Chat transitions read current config at action time. Window visibility is checked before dispatch. First mouse The custom button subclass accepts first mouse. Clicking an inactive footer button performs the action on the first physical click. The button itself does not become a window-drag region. Hit testing A click on the label, keycap, item wrapper, and button face resolves to the same button. Empty space does not resolve to the nearest action. Geometry is calculated in the correct coordinate system. Display scale does not leave stale pixel-space assumptions. Pass-through overlays left_info_view or equivalent passive overlays cannot steal footer item hits. Empty passive regions still allow intended window dragging. Native object lifecycle No leaked receiver, view, button, observer, or retained Objective-C object. Removed or hidden views cannot remain hit-testable. AppKit work remains on the main thread. Token and helper ownership Keycap placement uses footer_appkit_glyph_x, footer_appkit_glyph_y, and footer_keycap_padding_x_for_token. New colors, opacities, spacing, radii, and border behavior are either token-owned or explicitly justified as native geometry. No visual value is duplicated in a surface-local approximation. Glass lock No changed hunk retunes entry/exit duration, alpha, inset, blur, squish, envelope, fixture, or threshold. No test expectation was modified to accommodate a motion change. Use this changed-line scan as a prompt, not as proof: Bashgit -c color.ui=never diff \ --unified=0 \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- src/footer_popup.rs \ | rg \ '^\+.*(GLASS_|alpha|duration|blur|squish|inset|radius|padding|offset|0x[0-9A-Fa-f]{6}|NSMakeRect|setFrame)' \ > "$LANE/receipts/07-footer-new-values.txt" || true Source-audit test classification The current actions_button_visibility_tests.rs reads production source and searches for function names or substrings, including the footer dispatch, first-mouse subclass, geometry hit-test helpers, pass-through view, and callback wiring. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… +1 Audit the six-line deletion by comparing the exact base and candidate hunks: Bash{ echo "## Base reader sites" git show "$AUDIT_BASE:src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs" \ | rg -n 'read_to_string|read_all_rs_in_dir|include_str!|\.contains\(' || true echo echo "## Candidate reader sites" git show "$AUDIT_HEAD:src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs" \ | rg -n 'read_to_string|read_all_rs_in_dir|include_str!|\.contains\(' || true echo echo "## Exact diff" git -c color.ui=never diff \ --histogram \ --function-context \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs } > "$LANE/receipts/08-source-audit-delta.txt" For every changed test, record one of: PRUNED_BRITTLE_ASSERTION_WITHOUT_COVERAGE_LOSS TEST_WEAKENING TEST_REPOINTED_TO_CURRENT_OWNER FORMATTING_ONLY UNPROVEN Do not call any of these tests runtime or interaction proof. Work package 3 — Shared list-row semantics Path src/list_item_tests.rs Exact symbols The current file exercises: RowEligibility first_selectable_eligibility_index last_selectable_eligibility_index selectable_eligibility_index_at_or_before selectable_eligibility_index_at_or_after coerce_eligibility_selection format_shortcut_display should_show_row_shortcut should_show_search_shortcut should_show_search_description RowShortcutVisibilityPolicy LIST_ITEM_MOUSE_HOVER_TOOLTIPS_ENABLED These are ordinary unit tests rather than source-reading tests, so they are materially stronger for the pure functions they call. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… Exact audit Bashsource "$LANE/receipts/candidate.env" git -c color.ui=never diff \ --histogram \ --function-context \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- src/list_item_tests.rs \ > "$LANE/receipts/09-list-item-diff.patch" { echo "## Candidate list item owners" git show "$AUDIT_HEAD:src/list_item.rs" \ | rg -n \ 'RowEligibility|first_selectable_eligibility_index|last_selectable_eligibility_index|selectable_eligibility_index_at_or_before|selectable_eligibility_index_at_or_after|coerce_eligibility_selection|format_shortcut_display|should_show_row_shortcut|should_show_search_shortcut|should_show_search_description|RowShortcutVisibilityPolicy|LIST_ITEM_MOUSE_HOVER_TOOLTIPS_ENABLED' \ || true echo echo "## Consumers" rg -n \ 'coerce_eligibility_selection|RowShortcutVisibilityPolicy|should_show_row_shortcut|should_show_search_shortcut|should_show_search_description' \ src \ || true } > "$LANE/receipts/09-list-item-symbols-and-consumers.txt" Required scenarios Record whether the changed tests cover or omit: inert rows before, between, and after selectable rows; all-inert list; index beyond end after filtering; disabled explanatory row being focusable/selectable but not activatable; Enter/Space activation on a disabled explanatory row; list becoming empty while a stale selection remains; plus-delimited and space-delimited shortcuts; already-native symbols; unknown shortcut tokens; repeated delimiters and empty tokens; selected-only versus all-rows visibility; actual GPUI row focus and activation behavior. A pure helper test is C3 for the helper. It is only C2 for a real launcher or Actions-row behavior until a surface-level test crosses that boundary. Work package 4 — Agent Chat portal test support Path src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs Exact symbols Audit: parse_kind format_kind picker_query inline_target part_target dictation_part_token production_dictation_part part_inline_token clipboard_part_token replacement open_refusal parse_state format_state state_transition clear_terminal_state The helper delegates much of its behavior to production portal-contract functions, but it also maintains manual string-to-enum maps and fixture construction. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… Exact audit Bashsource "$LANE/receipts/candidate.env" git -c color.ui=never diff \ --histogram \ --function-context \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs \ > "$LANE/receipts/12-portal-diff.patch" rg -n \ 'test_support::agent_chat_portal|agent_chat_portal::|picker_query\(|inline_target\(|part_target\(|dictation_part_token\(|production_dictation_part\(|clipboard_part_token\(|state_transition\(|clear_terminal_state\(' \ src tests scripts \ > "$LANE/receipts/12-portal-consumers.txt" || true Required checks Every current ContextPortalKind variant that should be exposed by the harness has a parse_kind spelling. format_kind remains exhaustive. format_kind → parse_kind