nly exposure. Required real-boundary proof If the hunk changes what MCP clients can see or invoke, compilation and Rust tests are insufficient. Launch the frozen candidate and invoke the actual MCP computer-use request through the repository’s documented devtools path. First read the local runtime authority: Bashsed -n '1,280p' .agents/skills/script-kit-devtools/SKILL.md \ > "$LANE/receipts/14-script-kit-devtools-skill.txt" rg -n \ 'getElements|get_elements|computer|MCP|screenshot|click|launch|SCRIPT_KIT_TEST_STATUS' \ .agents/skills/script-kit-devtools/SKILL.md scripts/devtools scripts/agentic \ > "$LANE/receipts/14-runtime-harness-entrypoints.txt" || true Use the exact documented launch/client command discovered there. Record the literal command and complete raw request/response. Do not substitute a new ad hoc automation framework. The response must prove, when applicable: visible footer controls appear in the element tree; labels, roles, stable IDs, and enabled state match the renderer; a warning-banner dismiss control appears when the banner is visible; hidden or unsupported actions are not exposed as actionable; the same source that renders the element supplies the collector projection; no raw provider diagnostics, private note text, clipboard text, or unrelated sensitive state leaks through the new lines. The repository’s own AI reliability rule is blunt: if getElements cannot see a shared AI element, it is not proven. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… Work package 6 — Warning banner Path src/warning_banner.rs Exact symbols Audit: WarningBannerColors WarningBannerColors::from_theme WarningBannerColors::default OnClickCallback OnDismissCallback WarningBanner WarningBanner::new WarningBanner::on_click WarningBanner::on_dismiss WarningBanner::get_message WarningBanner::from_theme RenderOnce for WarningBanner The current component derives foreground from the warning color and uses the shared Button, but it also contains fixed element IDs and several direct visual values. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… The two-line package diff determines whether any of those are attributable to this branch. Exact audit Bashsource "$LANE/receipts/candidate.env" { echo "## Exact diff" git -c color.ui=never diff \ --histogram \ --function-context \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- src/warning_banner.rs echo echo "## Consumers" rg -n \ 'WarningBanner::|WarningBannerColors|warning-banner|warning-banner:dismiss' \ src tests scripts \ || true } > "$LANE/receipts/16-warning-banner-consumers.txt" Required scenarios Banner has on_click; click message area → parent callback fires once. Banner has on_click and on_dismiss; click dismiss → only dismiss callback fires. Banner lacks on_dismiss; dismiss control’s behavior is intentional rather than dead. Two banners render simultaneously → no duplicate-ID collision or wrong callback. Very long text truncates visually but remains available to accessibility tooling. Theme warning color changes → readable text and meaningful hover/focus state remain. Keyboard and accessibility users can identify and activate dismiss. Dismiss button and clickable parent do not create nested-action ambiguity. If no changed hunk affects any of these properties, record NO_MATERIAL_CHANGE rather than inheriting unrelated pre-existing debt as a branch regression. 5. Concrete high-risk failure matrix Every suspected issue in 03-breakage-candidates.md must use this form: exact path/symbol plus input or state → wrong output. These are the minimum scenarios to attempt. IDExact targetInput/stateWrong output or failureFT-01src/footer_popup.rs::footer_button_accepts_first_mouseScript Kit is inactive; user clicks Actions footer button onceApp merely activates; Actions does not open until a second clickFT-02footer_hit_test, footer_item_button_at_point, nearest_footer_item_buttonClick label, keycap, or wrapper edgeNo action, adjacent action, or arbitrary nearest action firesFT-03ensure_main_footer_action_listener, sync_main_footer_popupFull ↔ Mini ↔ Agent Chat transition repeated 20 times; click onceOne click dispatches twice or opens duplicate UIFT-04main_window_footer_config_with_cx, handle_main_footer_actionView changes after native footer config was renderedStale hidden action still executesFT-05FooterAction::Ai, open_tab_ai_agent_chat_with_entry_intentFresh launcher has an auto-selected first row; click Agent footer buttonAgent Chat opens with an implicit context chip or @cmd: mentionFT-06footer_button_mouse_down_can_move_windowDrag begins on button versus empty footer regionButton drags the window, or empty region fires an actionFT-07footer_item_button_at_pointMove window between 1× and 2× displays, then click slot edgesVisual and native hit rectangles divergeFT-08FooterAction::PasteResponseAgent Chat has no completed assistant response, or response changes between render and clickStale text is pasted, action remains enabled, or wrong turn is pastedFT-09install_footer_host_view and native view lifecycleHide/show or recreate main window repeatedlyOld invisible footer remains hit-testable or leaksLI-01RowEligibility callersDisabled explanation row is selected; press EnterDisabled row activates an operationLI-02coerce_eligibility_selection callerFiltering removes all selectable rows while selection remainsStale index highlights or activates a nonexistent rowLI-03format_shortcut_displayUnknown, repeated, or empty shortcut tokenMisleading or malformed keycap textPT-01parse_kindProduction adds a portal kind not added to harness parserHarness returns None and silently skips coveragePT-02clipboard_part_tokenTest asks for clipboard item B, while item A is currentHarness emits generic @clipboard and tests the wrong resourcePT-03production_dictation_partProduction validation depends on timestamp/duration/targetFixed fixture bypasses the branch being claimedMCP-01exact locally discovered symbolFooter or banner is visibleElement is absent from live MCP responseMCP-02exact locally discovered symbolHost callback is absent or action is unsupportedElement is exposed as enabled and actionableMCP-03exact locally discovered symbolMCP response is collected in Agent Chat or Notes contextPrivate/raw diagnostic text leaksWB-01WarningBanner::render dismiss closureBanner has parent click and dismiss callbacks; click ×Both callbacks fireWB-02fixed IDs in WarningBanner::renderTwo banners render at onceWrong dismiss target or duplicate element identityDOC-01changed GLOSSARY.md rowSource moved or behavior changedDocumentation points at nonexistent owner or overstates behaviorDOC-02changed CLAUDE.md instructionAgent follows document literallyBare Cargo, disabled flow dispatch, or invalid evidence claim results A breakage candidate without this concrete state transition belongs in 04-proof-gaps.md, not 03-breakage-candidates.md. 6. Confidence rubric Apply confidence per claim, never per file and never as a branch-wide average. LabelMeaningRequired evidencePermitted article wordingC4 — Runtime verifiedReal behavior crossed the live app, AppKit, OS, or MCP boundaryFrozen SHA, setup, raw trace/JSON, expected state transition, reproducible pass“Worked in the tested runtime states”C3 — Behavior verifiedFocused behavior/unit/integration test exercised the relevant logicNonzero test count, passing receipt, exact target and candidate SHA“The focused behavior test passed”C2 — Static verifiedDiff, type checking, source shape, docs link, or source-audit lock supports the claimFrozen source/diff plus successful compile or static checker“The source centralizes…” or “The static contract is present…”C1 — Concrete riskSource provides a plausible failure path, but it has not reproducedExact file/symbol and input → expected wrong output“Could regress…” or “Remains a breakage candidate…”C0 — UnverifiedSelf-report, prose, stale receipt, missing source, zero-test filter, or unsupported inferenceNone sufficient“Claimed but not proven” Disposition rules: VERIFIED_IMPROVEMENT: C3 or C4 and attributable to a changed hunk. PLAUSIBLE_IMPROVEMENT: C2 only. CONFIRMED_REGRESSION: deterministic C3 failure or C4 runtime reproduction. BREAKAGE_CANDIDATE: C1 or C2 concrete scenario without reproduction. PROOF_GAP: a material claim lacking the evidence tier its wording requires. A passing source-reading test cannot exceed C2. A screenshot alone cannot exceed C2 for interaction behavior. A zero-test Cargo filter is C0, even if Cargo exits successfully. A stale receipt from another SHA is C0 until rerun. 7. Bounded verification Use the local execution tool’s timeout facility. The timeout values below are hard ceilings, not estimates. V01 — Diff whitespace and conflict integrity Timeout: 15 seconds Bashsource "$LANE/receipts/candidate.env" git -c color.ui=never diff \ --check \ "$AUDIT_BASE" "$AUDIT_HEAD" -- \ CLAUDE.md \ GLOSSARY.md \ src/actions_button_visibility_tests.rs \ src/footer_popup.rs \ src/list_item_tests.rs \ src/mcp_computer_use_tools.rs \ src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs \ src/warning_banner.rs \ > "$LANE/receipts/01-diff-check.txt" 2>&1 Expected: exit 0, empty receipt. V02 — Glossary local-link checker Timeout: 20 seconds Run the Python checker in Work package 1. Expected: OK: <nonzero> local links; 0 missing paths; 0 stale numeric line anchors A passing link checker proves navigation only, not semantic accuracy. V03 — List-item unit tests Timeout: 180 seconds Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ test --lib 'list_item_tests::tests' -- --nocapture \ > "$LANE/receipts/09-list-item-tests.txt" 2>&1 Expected: nonzero tests executed; 0 failed; terminal includes test result: ok. running 0 tests is a proof gap. V04 — Footer/actions source-audit module Timeout: 240 seconds Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ test --lib 'actions_button_visibility_tests::tests' -- --nocapture \ > "$LANE/receipts/10-actions-source-audit-tests.txt" 2>&1 Expected: nonzero tests executed; 0 failed. Record the result as C2 static evidence only. V05 — Agent footer quick-question contract The footer’s Agent action is high risk because a fresh launcher normally has a real auto-selected row; quick-chat affordances must suppress that implicit context. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… Timeout: 180 seconds Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ test --lib 'quick_question_entry_suppresses_all_implicit_context' -- --nocapture \ > "$LANE/receipts/11-quick-question-contract.txt" 2>&1 Expected: exactly the named test runs and passes. This still does not prove the footer selects that entry intent; verify that at runtime. V06 — Portal-focused tests Timeout: 240 seconds First inspect 12-portal-consumers.txt. Then run the broadest still-focused existing Rust filter that actually contains the portal-contract tests: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ test --lib 'portal_contract' -- --nocapture \ > "$LANE/receipts/13-portal-tests.txt" 2>&1 Expected: nonzero tests, 0 failed. If it runs zero tests, run once with the exact locally discovered module/test filter from 12-portal-consumers.txt. That is the one permitted command-correction pass. V07 — MCP-focused tests Timeout: 240 seconds Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ test --lib 'mcp_computer_use_tools' -- --nocapture \ > "$LANE/receipts/15-mcp-tests.txt" 2>&1 Expected: nonzero matching tests and 0 failed. If zero tests run, record that explicitly and rely on check --lib plus the live MCP boundary. Do not invent a source-audit replacement. V08 — Warning-banner focused filter Timeout: 180 seconds Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ test --lib 'warning_banner' -- --nocapture \ > "$LANE/receipts/16-warning-banner-tests.txt" 2>&1 Expected: nonzero tests and 0 failed. A zero-test result is acceptable as a receipt but is a proof gap. V09 — Source-audit ratchet Timeout: 240 seconds Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ test --test source_audit_ratchet -- --nocapture \ > "$LANE/receipts/17-source-audit-ratchet.txt" 2>&1 Expected: all tests pass. Do not update an allowlist or expected source count to make it green. V10 — Library compile Timeout: 300 seconds Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ check --lib \ > "$LANE/receipts/18-check-lib.txt" 2>&1 Expected: exit 0 and terminal ends with a successful Finished line. V11 — Candidate runtime build Timeout: 420 seconds BashSCRIPT_KIT_AGENT_ARTIFACT_NAME=branch-trust-audit-06 \ ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ build --bin script-kit-gpui \ > "$LANE/receipts/18-runtime-build.txt" 2>&1 Expected: successful build and candidate artifact under: target-agent/artifacts/branch-trust-audit-06/script-kit-gpui Launch and automate it only through the documented script-kit-devtools workflow discovered earlier. Record the literal launch command and candidate SHA in 22-runtime-result.md. V12 — Conditional glass anti-drift Run only when the package diff or a related runtime failure implicates glass entry/exit/material values. Do not run it merely to decorate the audit. Timeout: 300 seconds per command Bashbun test \ scripts/devtools/glass-entry-motion-contract.test.ts \ scripts/devtools/glass-lifecycle-filmstrip.test.ts \ scripts/devtools/rapid-toggle-stress.test.ts \ > "$LANE/receipts/23-glass-antidrift-bun.txt" 2>&1 ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh \ test --lib \ 'platform::secondary_window_config_tests::glass_motion_fixture_matches_the_measured_production_calibration' \ -- --nocapture \ > "$LANE/receipts/23-glass-antidrift-cargo.txt" 2>&1 These are the repository-prescribed minimum anti-drift checks. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… INVALID_INTERFERENCE permits one quiet rerun. It is never a green product result. attachment-0001-9619f2c84b23eef… 8. Runtime footer matrix Write the complete setup, exact action, timestamped trace, result, and confidence into 06-runtime-matrix.md. Use neutral fixture data and no personal notes, clipboard history, or provider diagnostics. R01 — First click on inactive window Open full Script List with Actions available. Activate Finder or another app. Click the center of the Actions footer button once. Record: pre-click active application; click coordinates and target element; one footer-channel event; one canonical dispatch event; resulting Actions state. Pass: Script Kit becomes active and Actions opens from the same physical click. Exactly one action dispatch. Window does not move. R02 — Whole-item hit target For one footer item, click: button face; label; shortcut/keycap; left 10% of item wrapper; right 90% of item wrapper. Pass: All points inside the visible item invoke the same action exactly once. Points in the inter-item gap invoke nothing. R03 — Pass-through and drag behavior Drag from an empty footer/info region by at least 60 points. Drag from the center of a button by the same distance. Pass: Empty intended drag region moves the window without dispatch. Button click or press does not move the window. No action fires at drag end. R04 — Listener idempotence Perform 20 cycles: Full Script List → Mini → Full → Agent Chat → Back Then click Agent once. Pass: One channel event. One Agent Chat open. No duplicate window, duplicate context, or duplicate trace. Listener count remains one when observable. R05 — Current-config guard Render a footer state with an action. Transition to a view where that action should be absent. Click the old screen coordinates. Pass: No stale action executes. MCP element tree no longer advertises it. The current config is consulted at dispatch time. R06 — Agent button opens a clean quick question Return to a fresh launcher with the default first row visibly selected. Click the Agent footer button. Inspect composer and staged context. Pass: No implicit row context chip. No auto-inserted @cmd: mention. Agent Chat is otherwise usable. A failure here is a confirmed regression candidate even if the isolated quick-question unit test passes, because the footer may be invoking the wrong entry intent. R07 — Agent Chat response state Using a deterministic local/test response rather than a live provider call: before a response exists, verify Paste Response is absent or disabled; after a completed assistant response, verify it appears and pastes exactly that response; after a newer response, verify it does not paste stale content. R08 — Display and lifecycle At minimum: one 1× display state when available; one Retina/2× state; hide/show main window; close/reopen app window without terminating the process; move window between displays when available. Pass: Footer alignment and hit geometry remain coherent. No stale native view responds after removal. No visible layout jump is described as a motion proof. R09 — Live MCP projection Capture getElements before and after each of: full Script List; Mini; Actions open; Agent Chat; warning banner visible, when reachable. Save raw responses as 20-runtime-elements-before.json and 21-runtime-elements-after.json. Pass: visible actions appear with stable identity; hidden actions disappear; enabled state matches runtime capability; dismiss control appears when visible; no sensitive text leaks. 9. Screenshot request set Static screenshots must remain separate from 06-runtime-matrix.md. Each request states what the frame proves and what it cannot prove. When assigned, use these filenames: S06-01 — Full Script List footer .artifacts/branch-trust-audit/06-integrate-article/S06-01-script-list-full-footer.png Setup: neutral theme; full Script List; ordinary selected row with Actions available; footer fully visible; no personal script names or private data. Visual assertions: footer is visually detached; gutter is visible; labels and keycaps are legible; Run, Actions, and Agent configuration matches the current view; no clipped or overlapping item. Article caption: The native footer in full Script List mode. This frame verifies visible layout, labels, and spacing only; first-click delivery and action routing were tested separately. S06-02 — Mini footer configuration S06-02-script-list-mini-footer.png Visual assertions: Mini layout is active; footer contains only actions valid in Mini; no stale preview footer or duplicate Agent affordance. Caption: Mini mode after the footer rewrite. The image shows the view-specific configuration; it does not prove stale actions are rejected after a transition. S06-03 — Actions opened from footer S06-03-actions-open-via-footer.png Setup: capture immediately after a successful footer Actions click; keep selected row and Actions surface visible. Caption: The Actions surface reached through the footer’s canonical action path. The accompanying trace—not the screenshot—establishes that the click dispatched once. S06-04 — Clean Agent Chat entry S06-04-agent-chat-clean-entry.png Setup: fresh launcher initially has an auto-selected row; enter Agent Chat using the footer Agent button; composer is empty; no implicit context chip. Caption: Agent Chat opened from the footer without inheriting the launcher’s automatic selection. The runtime receipt records the entry intent and context state. S06-05 — Warning banner Conditional on the two-line change being materially relevant and a stable consumer being reachable. S06-05-warning-banner-theme-and-dismiss.png Caption: The shared warning banner under the tested theme. This frame verifies contrast, truncation, and visible dismiss affordance; event propagation and keyboard behavior require separate evidence. Screenshot manifest fields Every row in 07-screenshot-requests.md contains: shot_id candidate_sha finding_id owner_lane state_setup capture_boundary required_visible_elements proves does_not_prove privacy_scrub filename article_section caption status Do not publish a decorative screenshot without an attached finding or explanatory role. 10. Exact finding-artifact format Use this block in 02-observed-improvements.md, 03-breakage-candidates.md, and 04-proof-gaps.md. Markdown## 06-F### — <specific title> - Classification: VERIFIED_IMPROVEMENT | PLAUSIBLE_IMPROVEMENT | BREAKAGE_CANDIDATE | CONFIRMED_REGRESSION | PROOF_GAP - Confidence: C0 | C1 | C2 | C3 | C4 - Candidate SHA: <40-hex SHA> - Path: <exact path> - Symbol: <exact function/type/test/heading> - Changed hunk: <receipt path plus hunk heading or line range> - Input/state: <concrete setup> - Expected output: <observable result> - Observed output: <observable result or NOT RUN> - Attribution: <why this belongs to main...HEAD rather than pre-existing debt> - Static evidence: - <path> - Test evidence: - <path or NONE> - Runtime evidence: - <path or NONE> - Screenshot: - <shot ID or NONE> - What this proves: - <bounded statement> - What this does not prove: - <bounded statement> - Article-ready sentence: > <one publication-safe sentence> - Next action: - <exact card ID> - Future remediation: - <pseudodiff reference or NONE> A confirmed issue requires both attribution and an observable wrong result. A pre-existing problem belongs in a separate note marked PRE_EXISTING_CONTEXT, not in the branch regression count. 11. Conditional future-remediation pseudodiffs Do not apply these in this campaign. Include one in a finding only after its trigger is reproduced and source inspection confirms the named mechanism. PR-FT-01 — Button press incorrectly drags the window Trigger: R03 shows a button press moves the window; and footer_button_mouse_down_can_move_window currently returns the affirmative Objective-C value. Diff--- a/src/footer_popup.rs +++ b/src/footer_popup.rs @@ footer_button_mouse_down_can_move_window extern "C" fn footer_button_mouse_down_can_move_window( _this: &Object, _cmd: Sel, ) -> BOOL { - YES + NO } Verification affected: R01, R02, R03; footer-focused behavior test; no glass expectation changes. PR-FT-02 — Duplicate footer listener Trigger: R04 emits more than one action for one click; and ensure_main_footer_action_listener installs a new receiver/task on every sync. Diff--- a/src/app_impl/ui_window.rs +++ b/src/app_impl/ui_window.rs @@ struct ScriptListApp + main_footer_action_listener: Option<Task<()>>, @@ fn ensure_main_footer_action_listener - let receiver = crate::footer_popup::footer_action_channel(); - cx.spawn(/* listener body */).detach(); + if self.main_footer_action_listener.is_some() { + return; + } + + let receiver = crate::footer_popup::footer_action_channel(); + self.main_footer_action_listener = Some(cx.spawn(/* existing listener body */)); Required implementation detail: use the repository’s actual task/subscription type; clear or cancel it at the owning lifecycle boundary; do not add a second channel. Verification affected: R04; existing source lock around ensure_main_footer_action_listener; focused lifecycle test. PR-FT-03 — Geometry helper selects a button outside its item Trigger: R02 shows an inter-item gap or neighboring wrapper invokes an action; and the helper chooses a nearest button without proving the point is inside the item bounds. Diff--- a/src/footer_popup.rs +++ b/src/footer_popup.rs @@ fn footer_item_button_at_point - nearest_footer_item_button(hit_or_container) + for item in footer_hint_items(footer_hints_view) { + let local_point = convert_point_into_view(point, item); + if point_is_inside_bounds(local_point, item) { + return footer_button_in_subviews(item); + } + } + None Use the existing AppKit geometry helpers and types. Do not introduce an approximate distance threshold. Verification affected: R02; R07 display-scale case; test_native_footer_hit_test_resolves_whole_item_to_button. PR-PT-01 — Clipboard portal fixture discards required identity Trigger: production clipboard context is item-specific; a test requesting one item can resolve another because clipboard_part_token ignores id. Diff--- a/src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs +++ b/src/test_support/agent_chat_portal.rs @@ pub fn clipboard_part_token(id: &str) -> Option<String> { - let _ = id; - Some("@clipboard".to_string()) + let part = AiContextPart::ResourceUri { + uri: format!("kit://clipboard-history?id={id}"), + label: format!("Clipboard: {id}"), + }; + crate::ai::context_mentions::part_to_inline_token(&part) } Use the actual production URI and label constructor discovered locally. Do not invent a new URI form. Verification affected: portal round-trip tests; real context-selection harness; no production behavior change unless a separate production defect exists. PR-WB-01 — Multiple warning banners collide or dismiss is inaccessible Trigger: two banners reproduce duplicate identity/wrong callback; or getElements/accessibility inspection cannot identify the dismiss action. Diff--- a/src/warning_banner.rs +++ b/src/warning_banner.rs @@ pub struct WarningBanner { + id: SharedString, message: SharedString, ... } @@ -pub fn new(message: impl Into<SharedString>, colors: WarningBannerColors) -> Self { +pub fn new( + id: impl Into<SharedString>, + message: impl Into<SharedString>, + colors: WarningBannerColors, +) -> Self { Self { + id: id.into(), message: message.into(), ... } } @@ fn render -Button::new("warning-banner:dismiss", "×", dismiss_colors) +Button::new( + format!("{}:dismiss", self.id), + "×", + dismiss_colors, +) +/* use the existing Button accessibility-label API: + "Dismiss warning" */ Verification affected: banner consumer compile sites; multiple-banner test; keyboard/accessibility runtime check; MCP element projection. MCP remediation rule Do not prewrite an MCP pseudodiff. The provided sources do not expose the changed symbol. A future MCP remediation entry must quote the exact locally observed function or serializer and replace only the failing three-line mechanism. 12. Integrated path accounting and lane reconciliation This package owns the final coverage proof, but it must not trust sibling worker-report.md prose. Required sibling interface Each lane must expose a path-accounting.tsv with at least: path lane status disposition finding_ids evidence_paths confidence candidate_sha For this lane, either make 01-path-accounting.tsv conform directly or generate a lane-local adapter. Union check After all lane ledgers exist, run a lane-local Python reconciliation that: loads every lane path-accounting.tsv; rejects any row whose candidate_sha differs from AUDIT_HEAD; rejects duplicate ownership unless an explicit shared-owner field exists; computes the expected 481 paths directly from frozen Git; writes union, gaps, and duplicates under this lane; exits nonzero on any gap or unexplained duplicate. Bashexport AUDIT_HEAD AUDIT_BASE LANE python3 - <<'PY' import csv import os import subprocess import sys from collections import defaultdict from pathlib import Path head = os.environ["AUDIT_HEAD"] base = os.environ["AUDIT_BASE"] lane_dir = Path(os.environ["LANE"]) lanes_root = lane_dir.parent expected = set( subprocess.check_output( ["git", "diff", "--name-only", base, head], text=True, ).splitlines() ) ledger_paths = sorted(lanes_root.glob("*/path-accounting.tsv")) if not ledger_paths: print("No lane path-accounting.tsv files found", file=sys.stderr) sys.exit(1) rows = [] owners = defaultdict(list) for ledger in ledger_paths: with ledger.open(newline="") as handle: reader = csv.DictReader(handle, delimiter="\t") required = { "path", "lane", "status", "disposition", "finding_ids", "evidence_paths", "confidence", "candidate_sha", } missing = required - set(reader.fieldnames or []) if missing: raise SystemExit(f"{ledger}: missing columns {sorted(missing)}") for row in reader: if row["candidate_sha"] != head: raise SystemExit( f"{ledger}: stale candidate for {row['path']}: " f"{row['candidate_sha']} != {head}" ) rows.append(row) owners[row["path"]].append(row["lane"]) actual = set(owners) gaps = sorted(expected - actual) extra = sorted(actual - expected) duplicates = sorted( (path, lane_names) for path, lane_names in owners.items() if len(set(lane_names)) > 1 ) union_path = lane_dir / "receipts/90-integrated-path-union.tsv" with union_path.open("w", newline="") as handle: writer = csv.DictWriter( handle, fieldnames=[ "path", "lane", "status", "disposition", "finding_ids", "evidence_paths", "confidence", "candidate_sha", ], delimiter="\t", lineterminator="\n", ) writer.writeheader() for row in sorted(rows, key=lambda value: value["path"]): writer.writerow(row) (lane_dir / "receipts/91-integrated-path-gaps.txt").write_text( "\n".join(gaps + [f"EXTRA\t{path}" for path in extra]) + ("\n" if gaps or extra else "") ) (lane_dir / "receipts/92-integrated-path-duplicates.txt").write_text( "\n".join(f"{path}\t{','.join(names)}" for path, names in duplicates) + ("\n" if duplicates else "") ) print(f"expected={len(expected)}") print(f"accounted={len(actual)}") print(f"gaps={len(gaps)}") print(f"extra={len(extra)}") print(f"duplicates={len(duplicates)}") if len(expected) != 481 or gaps or extra or duplicates: sys.exit(1) PY Expected: expected=481 accounted=481 gaps=0 extra=0 duplicates=0 Evidence reconciliation rules For every sibling finding selected for the article: candidate SHA must match; evidence path must exist; terminal receipt must include command and result; screenshot must include state setup and bounded claim; runtime claim must contain a real boundary artifact; conflicting findings remain separate until the smallest common falsifier is rerun; strongest evidence wins confidence, but weaker contradictory evidence is retained in the ledger; missing or stale evidence downgrades the finding to C0 rather than disappearing it. Record all downgrades in 10-integration-reconciliation.md. 13. Patch-ready article narrative Article structure Use this exact order: Markdown# The Branch Is a Claim, Not a Result ## 50 Commits, 481 Paths, and a Trust Problem ## How We Audited Without Trusting the Audit ## What the Evidence Actually Supports ### Verified Improvements ### Plausible Improvements ### Breakage Candidates ### Unproven AI Claims ## Screenshots: What They Show—and What They Cannot ## The Executable Next-Steps Program ## Coverage and Receipts ## The Executable Next-Steps Program must be the largest substantive section: at least 45% of the article body and longer than the four findings subsections combined. Suggested body allocation: opening and scale: 